# Placed shapes in Inbox/Shapes.canvas, which tests/drive.rs writes first: a Venn (a text node
# with cold-lava's field) and a plain card. Another program saves the file the way Obsidian
# does, nodes sorted and positions rounded, and keeps the field: nothing is lost. Then one saves
# it without the field: the whiteboard says so until a key, keeps the shape and saves it back.
# tests/drive.rs reads the file after.
size 100x30
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
wait-for example-workspace
keys w
wait-for whiteboards · type to filter · ⏎ open · Esc back
type shapes
keys enter
wait-for whiteboard Shapes · 2 cards · 0 arrows
write Inbox/Shapes.canvas {"nodes":[\n{"id":"plain","type":"text","text":"Plain","x":400,"y":0,"width":200,"height":100},\n{"id":"venn","type":"text","text":"Simple Venn diagram","x":0,"y":0,"width":301,"height":300,"cold-lava":{"shape":"venn2","rotation":15,"exact":[0.4,0,300.5,300]}}\n],"edges":[],"cold-lava-version":1}\n
wait-for merged changes made outside cold-lava
expect-not lost cold-lava's fields
write Inbox/Shapes.canvas {"nodes":[\n{"id":"plain","type":"text","text":"Plain","x":400,"y":0,"width":200,"height":100},\n{"id":"venn","type":"text","text":"Simple Venn diagram","x":50,"y":0,"width":301,"height":300}\n],"edges":[]}\n
wait-for lost cold-lava's fields on 1 shape
keys space
wait-gone lost cold-lava's fields
keys q
wait-for cold-lava workspaces
keys q
exits 0
